WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.880
- So, The Carters just
released their joint album,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.600
Everything is Love,
completely unannounced,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.890
and with it, came a brand new music video.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.430
- This time, they rented out
The Louvre, which, how Sway?

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.200
The Louvre and its international art

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.080
serve as the foundation for a ton

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.870
of themes in this music video.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.350
Here are some of the symbols
that you might have missed.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.860
- While Beyonce is known for having

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.380
high energy performances
throughout her videos,

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.350
in Apeshit, most of her movements

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.210
are actually pretty subdued.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.470
The Carters are purposely statuesque,

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.780
barely moving, in front of one of the most

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.330
recognizable portraits of
all time, the Mona Lisa.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.337
The Carters are literally living art,

00:00:40.337 --> 00:00:42.170
and the three faces in the frame

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.570
are portrayed as legendary equals.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.230
The two live up to this
particular comparison.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.630
Art history grad student, Heidi Herrera,

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.590
noted that people around the world flock

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.830
to both the Mona Lisa and the Carters,

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.540
just for something as
simple as a quick picture.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.490
Vulture points out that
throughout the video,

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.440
the duo continues to make classical

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.010
art come to life in brand new contexts.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.410
Like Beyonce dancing as
Nike, the Greek goddess

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.020
of victory for you know, obvious reasons,

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.130
or when she reigned with her fellow female

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.020
dancers in front of The
Coronation of Napoleon.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.290
The painting depicts
Napoleon crowning his wife,

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.250
Josephine, the first
empress of the French.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.030
She switches to a nude
wardrobe and lioness hair

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.620
to dance in front of The
Great Sphinx of Tanis,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.180
and pulls her hair back to
wine in front of Venus de Milo.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.390
One of the most important
artistic references

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.780
was when Jay-Z did his verse
in front of The Raft of Medusa.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.650
The painting shows the
aftermath of a French tragedy,

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.520
where a naval boat crashed
due to poor navigation,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.440
leading to a number of deaths.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.200
Out of the 150 plus crew members,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.050
17 decided to stay, and 15 survived.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.640
The moment captured in the painting

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.020
was when the crew members
saw the rescue ship,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.697
after 13 days with little to no food.

00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:56.750
This hope, after the turmoil,
and the determination

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.720
to stay, symbolizes
where Beyonce and Jay-Z

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.430
are in their relationship right now.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.050
They went through hell,
but they persevered.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.410
- Now, let's get into the cultural

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.990
significance of the video.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.570
There's one overarching theme,

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.630
and that's black excellence.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:14.040
First, let's talk about the
portrait of Madame Recamier.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.600
The woman depicted in the painting

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.400
was the wife of a banker
and a huge socialite.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.290
Putting black women in front of this piece

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.392
signifies how black women
themselves are iconic.

00:02:23.392 --> 00:02:26.370
The styling of the women
is also significant.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.140
It's reminiscent of French artist,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.580
Marie Benoit's Portrait of a Black Woman.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.340
This kind of depiction of a black woman

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.740
was rare for its time
period, and historians

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.580
believed it was painted in
support of abolitionism.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.160
Keep in mind that The Louvre houses

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.300
a lot of art from the Napoleonic era.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.520
Of course, we know Napoleon as one of the

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.990
most prominent colonizers in history.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.270
It's no accident that Jay and Bey position

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.030
themselves as art, in the
midst of these colonial relics.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.710
They've literally colonized The Louvre,

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.740
to celebrate who and what they are.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.430
This painting here, depicts a woman

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.650
caressing a man with a stab wound,

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.782
and it's imitated in the video
by this black man and woman.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.700
The stab wound is representative

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.130
of police brutality against blacks,

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.130
which brings us to the image of black men

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.980
kneeling outside of the museum,

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.640
a reference to Colin Kaepernick's protest.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.610
Black women swoop and sway
among the white marble floors

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:20.020
as Beyonce sings, "I
can't believe we made it."

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.210
It's a celebration of success
in the face of oppression,

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.250
and these images of black bodies in this

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.870
historically white space emphasize that.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.620
- Did you see anything
we might have missed?

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.340
Let us know in the comments below.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.990
- And subscribe to Insider
for more video breakdowns.

